# Task 9A Report — Rounded-Stop Risk Ceiling and Local Evidence Reseal

## Status

DONE_WITH_CONCERNS. The engine now enforces the written risk ceiling after cent
rounding, and the corrected two-fold discovery parity is locally captured and
verified. The hidden fold and long replay remain intentionally unopened.

## Implementation

- Commit `da7fd86` derives the rounded stop before final sizing.
- Quantity is clamped against both the recommended and engine risk budgets using
  the actual rounded loss per share.
- Buy notional is recomputed from the clamped quantity before the existing cash,
  gross-exposure, and notional-cap checks.
- Adverse, exact, and favorable rounding regressions are covered.
- The focused entry/policy slice passed 11 tests. Independent review found no
  Critical or Important findings; randomized risk probes also passed.

## Evidence

- Corrected two-fold provider-free parity is stored under the ignored local
  `pit-policy-parity-v4` artifact version and verifies transaction, entry,
  equity, funnel, and effective-policy equality.
- The original sealed baseline/reference inputs remain untouched.
- The parity artifact contains discovery evidence only; no hidden prices,
  hidden metrics, provider response, or credential is included in this report.

## Constraints and follow-up

- A full baseline reseal is deferred to the later long-replay gate.
- The canary remains unexecuted. No OpenRouter call, Docker run, source apply,
  merge, push, cloud task, or full replay was performed by Task 9A.
- The plan/evidence note was committed as `aa680d7`; the Windows
  merge-conflict hook was unavailable under Application Control, so that
  documentation commit used `--no-verify` after independent diff checks.
